WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.910
My phone can chat with me all day.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.860
But when I asked it about tomorrow’s

3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.460
weather, it just made up an answer!

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.250
A real helper would go and check.

5
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.620
But how?

6
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.340
Today: helpers that do

7
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.880
things, not just talk.

8
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.250
Some AI helpers only talk.

9
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.170
You ask, and they write words back.

10
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.380
On their own, they can’t check

11
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.780
anything or do anything.

12
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.960
Other helpers can use tools.

13
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.540
A tool is a small program that does

14
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.600
one job: it tells the weather, does

15
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.420
sums, or sets a reminder.

16
00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.340
These helpers are called agents.

17
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.330
An agent is an AI helper that

18
00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.450
uses tools to get a job done.

19
00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.350
It listens, makes a plan, uses a

20
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.170
tool, and then answers.

21
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.000
Darsi Tiny is a small helper

22
00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.460
that lives on a phone.

23
00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.910
I asked it: what’s the

24
00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.490
weather in Kafi tomorrow?

25
00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.050
First it made a plan: check the weather.

26
00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:09.670
Then it used the weather tool.

27
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.260
The tool sent back the facts:

28
00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.860
sunny, thirty-five degrees, and

29
00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.980
a small chance of rain.

30
00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:19.190
Then Darsi Tiny answered with those facts.

31
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.760
It didn’t guess: it checked!

32
00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:23.550
Quick check!

33
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.170
Which of these helpers is an

34
00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.770
agent that uses a tool?

35
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.730
The weather helper.

36
00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.830
It uses a tool to check, then

37
00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.590
answers from what the tool said.

38
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.590
Telling a joke or saying hello

39
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.330
needs no tool at all.

40
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.740
In the app, pick a

41
00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.200
question and tap One step.

42
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.510
Watch the plan, the tool and the

43
00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:49.650
answer appear, one by one.

44
00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.090
Ask a grown-up first, because

45
00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.810
the helper downloads once.

46
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:55.930
Your turn.

47
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.430
A helper says it will be sunny tomorrow,

48
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.710
but it never used the weather tool.

49
00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.450
Should you believe it?

50
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.930
Not yet: it didn’t check with a tool.

51
00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.590
Remember: some helpers only

52
00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.130
talk, while agents use tools.

53
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.040
An agent listens, plans, uses

54
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.000
a tool, then answers.

55
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.440
Try it yourself: play Helper

56
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.680
and Tool with a friend.

57
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.720
Your friend asks about

58
00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.780
the class timetable.

59
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.670
You make a plan, then ask the tool:

60
00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.070
someone holding the timetable.

61
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.540
Then answer from what the tool said!
